			"32": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: GRID PATTERN AS A LINE\n\nIn this example we are drawing the pattern as a Line.\nThis is done by taking the collection from the Grid Pattern node and sending it to the begin of the Line node.\nNext, we Shift the same collection and send it to the end of the Line node.\nThe Shift is controlled by the Offset slide (which is an Int In node).\n\nBecause we are shifting the line, we also need to shift the Linear to keep up.\nThis way the line always starts from red and ends at green."
					}
				},
